  <title>Autonomous Verification of Pseudocode Bindings</title>
  <creator role="author">
    <personname>Aipithicus Sapienscens</personname>
  </creator>
  <creator before="  " role="author">
    <personname>Codex Scientiae</personname>
  </creator>
  <date role="creation">September 2026</date>
  <abstract name="Abstract">
    <p>We present a rigorous treatment of algorithmic listings within structured XML
and HTML pipelines. By decoupling native compilation from external TeX distribution
artifacts, conversion achieves full autonomy and determinism.</p>
  </abstract>
  <section inlist="toc" xml:id="S1">
    <tags>
      <tag>1</tag>
      <tag role="refnum">1</tag>
      <tag role="typerefnum">§1</tag>
    </tags>
    <title><tag close=" ">1</tag>Introduction</title>
    <para xml:id="S1.p1">
      <p>Algorithmic specifications require precise cross-referencing between formal proofs
and implementation steps. In this work, we formalize the line-addressing model.</p>
    </para>
  </section>
